ARCHITECTURE DIAGRAM DESCRIPTION (PLACEHOLDER CONTENT)

Flow:
Camera -> AI Service -> Backend API -> MySQL Database
                             |
                             -> Frontend Dashboard (React)

Component responsibilities:

1) Camera Layer
- Captures live video frames
- Provides source input to AI service

2) AI Service (Python)
- Reads frames from camera
- Detects faces and recognizes students
- Batches attendance events
- Sends events to backend endpoint (/api/attendance/ai)

3) Backend API (Spring Boot)
- Handles authentication and JWT security
- Exposes APIs for auth, students, attendance, summaries
- Validates and stores attendance events
- Applies role-based access control

4) Database (MySQL)
- Stores users, students, attendance
- Supports querying by date/student/class

5) Frontend (React + TypeScript)
- Login/logout and token handling
- Student CRUD and filtering
- Attendance view, summary, manual marking
- Dashboard metrics and recent records

Deployment:
- Services can run locally or via Docker Compose
- AI service can be deployed on Raspberry Pi edge device
